<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">O'Connor Faly</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ua Conchobair Failge</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The O'Connors Faly, Ua Conchobair Failge, were the ruling family of Uí Failge in the Irish midlands from the 11th century to the 1550s. They held out against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-normans">Anglo-Normans</a>, raided the Pale and took black rent from its settlers. Their lordship was confiscated after risings in the 1540s and shired as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-offaly">King's County</a> in 1556.</p></div>
